cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Awesome Single-Cell QC: a catalog of single-cell QC and preprocessing tools, methods and evidence"
message: "If you use this catalog, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Barker
    given-names: Harlan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4125-2522"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thirtysix/awesome-single-cell-qc"
abstract: >-
  A hand-curated catalog of single-cell QC and preprocessing tools, methods and
  evidence, with an emphasis on salvaging cells and signal in multiplexed
  experiments, plus a map of the adjacent analysis steps that QC choices feed
  into. Every record carries an evidence tier, the side it works on (keeping or
  removing cells), its required inputs and, where it recovers cells or signal,
  the reported gain and who measured it. Identifiers are verified against
  Crossref and PubMed; citation counts come from OpenAlex.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - quality control
  - preprocessing
  - demultiplexing
  - cell hashing
  - doublet detection
  - ambient RNA
  - multiplexed drug screens
  - bioinformatics software
license: CC-BY-4.0
references:
  - type: database
    title: "OpenAlex"
    url: "https://openalex.org"
    notes: "Source of citation counts (CC0)."
